Keep <immintrin.h> in sync with the __AVX__ guard in MemCopy64.

The port forces -DSNAPPY_HAVE_X86_CRC32=OFF and -DSNAPPY_HAVE_BMI2=OFF in
portfile.cmake, so the include below is dropped, but the 64-byte copy further
down is selected by the live target macro __AVX__ instead of those cached
variables. Any toolchain whose default ISA already has AVX therefore compiles
the AVX branch without the intrinsic declarations:

  snappy.cc:1242:3: error: '__m256i' was not declared in this scope

Extend the include guard with the exact condition the copy site uses. Targets
without AVX keep the current behaviour (the branch stays preprocessed out);
targets with AVX get the header the branch requires.

--- a/snappy.cc
+++ b/snappy.cc
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
 #endif
 #endif  // !defined(SNAPPY_HAVE_NEON_CRC32)
 
-#if SNAPPY_HAVE_BMI2 || SNAPPY_HAVE_X86_CRC32
+#if SNAPPY_HAVE_BMI2 || SNAPPY_HAVE_X86_CRC32 || (defined(__x86_64__) && defined(__AVX__))
 // Please do not replace with <x86intrin.h>. or with headers that assume more
 // advanced SSE versions without checking with all the OWNERS.
 #include <immintrin.h>
